    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today, as our core offensive engines\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014are all sidelined by team off-days, forcing us to rely on our secondary depth to navigate the 5x5 categories. Given the scarcity of stolen bases, our primary objective is to maximize speed-threat efficiency; however, the board is thin today. **Jorge Polanco** represents our most reliable, albeit marginal, start with a score of 51.86. While he holds a neutral-to-slight advantage hitting against Aaron Nola, he remains a \"start only\" option pending official lineup confirmation, as his value is tethered to his spot in the middle of the order. The 31% rain risk in Philadelphia adds a layer of volatility that could further cap his output if the game is shortened or delayed.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom narrowly missed the cut due to unfavorable park factors and unfavorable matchups against high-xERA arms that suppressed their upside below our 60-point threshold. We remain particularly cautious regarding **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to occupy a roster spot while on the IL; his absence remains our biggest hurdle in reclaiming ground in the SB category. With the likes of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Josh Lowe** also inactive or failing to clear the bench floor today, we are effectively playing a defensive rotation. We are banking on **Jorge Polanco** to provide enough stability to bridge the gap until the full lineup returns, though we remain wary of the atmospheric risks surrounding his matchup.",
